		{"type":"file","file":"Renderer.md","id":"4c7970e4acd935b6","x":3040,"y":550,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"type":"file","file":"Utils.md","id":"a4bcf37235bdb626","x":1240,"y":-400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"type":"file","file":"Buffer.md","id":"62d79a29ddf57d88","x":1720,"y":-400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"type":"file","file":"Pipeline.md","id":"d1cef588311cbb2d","x":1300,"y":1580,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Vertex and Index Buffer</h1>\n\nAlso called VBO or IBO, Contains the data that will be sent through the graphics pipeline","id":"31b4588514be2f58","x":-1080,"y":-540,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Input Assembler</h1>\n\nCollects raw vertex data from the buffers, may also use an index buffer to repeat certain elements without having to duplicate the vertex data.","id":"db26db07a943e6f7","x":-1080,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Vertex Shader</h1>\n\nIs run for every vertex, used to apply transformations (model space to screen space) and passes per-vertex data down the pipeline","id":"41e57e8e721413d5","x":-1080,"y":-90,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Tesselation</h1>\n\nUsed to subdivide geometry based on a set of rules to increase mesh geometry","id":"03c413c2681a2990","x":-1080,"y":130,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Geometry Shader</h1>\n\nIs run on every primitive (triangle, line, point), similar to tessellation but more flexible. Nos used much as the performance are not good","id":"36ec642f57955c78","x":-1080,"y":350,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Rasterization</h1>\n\nDiscretizes the primitives into fragments. Which are the pixel elements that will fill the frame buffer. Discards fragments outside the screen and usually fragments behind other fragments (depth testing). Data outputted by the vertex shader are interpolated across the fragments","id":"41b51d2f3c3d742f","x":-1080,"y":570,"width":380,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Fragment Shader</h1>\n\nIs run for every fragment, determines which frame buffer(s) the fragments are written to and with which color and depth values. Uses interpolated data from the vertex shader.","id":"8be1e57181afcd6f","x":-1080,"y":850,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Color Blending</h1>\n\nApplies operations to mix different fragments that map the same pixel in the frame buffer. Fragments can overwrite each other, add up or be mixed (based upon transparency for example)","id":"5c739b862553e1b6","x":-1080,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"type":"text","text":"<h1 align=\"center\">Frame Buffer</h1>\n\nFinal result of a frame, contains fragment colors but can also contain other per fragment data like the depth","id":"0af8fa12f77a0459","x":-1080,"y":1290,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"2"},
		{"type":"file","file":"RenderSystem.md","id":"de35552e17eb6cac","x":1300,"y":2130,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"type":"text","text":"## Legend\n- 🟣: Pre-Pipeline, Application input\n- 🔴: Programmable modules\n- 🟢: Fixed Modules\n- 🟡: Output","id":"a5b05cb513729406","x":-510,"y":1260,"width":460,"height":190},
		{"type":"file","file":"SwapChain.md","id":"6324890a1f251016","x":2180,"y":2350,"width":400,"height":400},
